46301 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446301 1077 "selection" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446301 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446248 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446301 1079 #uuid "e40c8c90-6ba2-519b-a998-3dcd473e1e7c" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446302 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446298 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446302 1069 "q-72692" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446302 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446302 1071 "The city of Baku, in Azerbaijan, is $91.8$ feet below sea level, while the city of Porto Alegre, in Brazil, is $16.4$ feet above sea level. What is the difference between the elevations of both cities?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446302 1072 #uuid "090aa86c-d0e1-50e4-9098-0d31886c4162" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446302 1074 "To calculate the difference between the elevations of both cities, we must calculate the difference between the city with the highest elevation and the city with the lowest elevation. That is, we must calculate $16.4-(-91.8).$ This gives\n\n$$\n16.4-(-91.8)=16.4+91.8=108.2\\,\\text{ft}.\n$$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446303 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446296 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446303 1069 "q-72689" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446303 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446303 1071 "Noah removes some food from his freezer to defrost. The temperature of the food was $-{4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ After a few hours, the temperature of the food increased by ${10.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ What was the temperature of the food after those few hours?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446303 1072 #uuid "1b039dc7-fa95-5b45-bb27-8c6ed8ecbe43" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446303 1074 "To determine the temperature of the food after a few hours, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the food. This gives\n\n$$\n-{4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{10.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={5.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the food after a few hours was ${5.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446304 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446295 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446304 1069 "q-68927" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446304 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446304 1071 "As a part of a scientific experiment, Santiago placed a liquid, whose initial temperature was ${15.3}^{∘}\\text{C}$, into a refrigerator. After an hour, he removed the liquid from the refrigerator and placed it on a table. He observed that its temperature decreased by ${17.1}^{∘}\\text{C}.$\n\nAfter $15$ minutes, Santiago measured the temperature of the liquid again and concluded that it increased by ${6}^{∘}\\text{C}.$ What was the final temperature of the liquid?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446304 1072 #uuid "241ae34a-170c-5ddb-b291-a82fcffae551" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446304 1074 "First, we must determine the temperature of the liquid when removing it from the refrigerator. Since its temperature decreased by ${17.1}^{∘}\\text{C}$ compared to its initial temperature, we must subtract the variation in temperature from the initial temperature. This gives\n\n$$\n{15.3}^{∘}\\text{C}-{17.1}^{∘}\\text{C}=-{1.8}^{∘}\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature of the liquid after the $15$ minutes outside the refrigerator. Since the temperature of the liquid increased by ${6}^{∘}\\text{C}$ compared to the temperature it had when it was removed from the refrigerator, we add the variation in temperature to the temperature of the liquid when it was removed from the refrigerator. This gives\n\n$$\n-{1.8}^{∘}\\text{C}+{6}^{∘}\\text{C}={4.2}^{∘}\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final temperature of the liquid was ${4.2}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446305 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446293 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446305 1069 "q-72687" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446305 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446305 1071 "The average temperature in the Arctic in December of a particular year was ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ Due to plummeting temperatures in the winter, the average temperature in February of the next year decreased by ${6.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to the average temperature in December. What was the average temperature in the Arctic in February?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446305 1072 #uuid "3b6c17fd-0ff9-5d87-b06b-efe5f60e73d4" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446305 1074 "To determine the average temperature of the Arctic in February, we subtract the change in temperature (from December to February) from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n{3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{6.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the average temperature in the Arctic at the end of February was $-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446306 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446299 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446306 1069 "q-72699" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446306 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446306 1071 "In Oslo, Norway, the average temperature in November is ${3.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ In January, the average temperature decreases by ${6.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November. Finally, in March, the average temperature increases by ${4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to January. Determine the average temperature in Oslo in March." 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446306 1072 #uuid "7e4b7794-21eb-5f19-b665-c965b7cd7892" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446306 1074 "First, we must determine the average temperature in Oslo during the month of January. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${6.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in November. This gives\n\n$$\n{3.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{6.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{2.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature during the month of March. Since we know that the temperature increases on average by ${4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to January, we add the variation in temperature to the average temperature in January. This gives\n\n$$\n-{2.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Oslo in March is ${1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446307 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446297 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446307 1069 "q-72694" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446307 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446307 1071 "On a certain day in December $2019,$ the temperature in Toronto (Ontario) was $-{7.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ That same day, the temperature in Seattle (Washington) was ${3.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ How many degrees higher was Seattle's temperature compared to the temperature in Toronto?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446307 1072 #uuid "90030a66-0035-58a4-bb92-3cb6359f5340" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446307 1074 "To find how many degrees higher Seattle's temperature was compared to the temperature in Toronto, we must calculate the difference between the temperatures of Seattle and Toronto. This gives\n\n$$\n{3.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-(-{7.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C})={3.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{7.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={11.0}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446308 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446300 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446308 1069 "q-68475" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446308 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446308 1071 "An airplane flies over the Pacific Ocean at $850$ meters above sea level. At the same time, a submarine is in the ocean at $125$ meters below sea level. What is the difference in the altitude of the submarine compared to the airplane?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446308 1072 #uuid "bea699ae-050c-5792-a06d-737fb3226f50" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446308 1074 "To determine how far below the submarine is compared to the airplane, we must calculate the difference between the location of the submarine and the location of the plane. This gives\n\n$$\n850-(-125)=850+125=975.\n$$\n\nThus, the submarine is $975\\,\\text{m}$ below the airplane." 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446309 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446294 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446309 1069 "q-72690" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446309 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446309 1071 "Ffion has an authorized overdraft facility with her bank. Her bank balance on Monday was $-$43.74.$ To reduce her debt, Ffion decides to make a deposit of $$29.50$ into her bank account on the following Wednesday. What was Ffion's balance at the end of the day on Wednesday?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446309 1072 #uuid "eee9ef15-a1f2-573e-9281-9406377c6d0e" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446309 1074 "To determine the balance at the end of the day on Wedensday, we must add the amount of money Ffion deposited to the starting balance. This gives\n\n$$\n-$43.74+$29.50=-$14.24\n$$\n\nThus, Ffion's balance at the end of the day on Wednesday was $-$14.24.$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446310 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446301 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446310 1069 "q-68865" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446310 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446310 1071 "Angela has a bank account with ASB Bank, and she has an overdraft facility authorized by this bank. At the start of a certain week, her balance was $$75.75.$ At the end of that week, she decided to withdraw $$80$ to buy a sound system. What was Angela's balance at the end of that week?" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446310 1072 #uuid "fdddf3b8-a8e2-50b7-b535-a38f81b62fbd" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true] [17592186446310 1074 "To find Angela's bank balance at the end of that week, we subtract the amount of money she withdrew from the starting balance. This gives\n\n$$\n$75.75-$80=-$4.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Angela's bank balance at the end of the week was $-$4.25.$" 13194139534973 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00da30b5-b3d0-5bfc-9108-1748d1ef8161" 17592186446248 "answer-09c7887f-43ee-5006-a75e-672b5588253f" 17592186446249 "answer-0eb9330e-51f7-5baa-bc8f-ef79483df4a3" 17592186446250 "answer-14c45106-8c1e-5023-a95b-972641309ade" 17592186446251 "answer-1901839c-9a23-56ef-9d4a-3bdd2ed62c10" 17592186446252 "answer-1b2918c8-4bdf-5a95-acb9-70cc67316e8b" 17592186446253 "answer-1c858a58-aaea-50a9-b348-cced1f37edc1" 17592186446254 "answer-1f6f34e7-af0a-5515-ac9b-aab27c95e173" 17592186446255 "answer-2a92ffa2-e67b-5d1d-93bc-87b38d849626" 17592186446256 "answer-2cdba9bd-4453-5061-af15-1266f0456210" 17592186446257 "answer-2e0910d5-5b9a-59d4-9b25-cd2e01d514e5" 17592186446258 "answer-2edce43b-e6b5-5105-88fc-e87dc8066cde" 17592186446259 "answer-38d4b685-1f6a-5047-b1ad-fcda22849885" 17592186446260 "answer-3d8e357e-5a75-51e0-975a-7fc507bde8c3" 17592186446261 "answer-3da138ba-fd75-53d0-b4e4-20f9484e97d7" 17592186446262 "answer-4094736e-df60-54b8-9c50-37ff990fb2b5" 17592186446263 "answer-4a5ecfb1-81e3-578f-8bc4-593731a199e8" 17592186446264 "answer-4ca87e66-4ef9-5a01-9d25-9e7126c88980" 17592186446265 "answer-56c45950-130f-53fe-a976-47b21989b82b" 17592186446266 "answer-669006a1-5ff4-5271-9a2c-40bb3c7733d1" 17592186446267 "a